// spec: §6.2.7 §6.2.14
// expect-error: `#[deprecated_safe]` cannot be attached to a struct; it goes on a function, a method, an extern function or a static
// expect-error: malformed `#[deprecated]`: expected no argument, a message string, or `(since = "0.1.6", note = "..")`

// `#[deprecated_safe]` goes on functions and statics; `since` is a release.
#[deprecated_safe]
struct S { v: i32; }

#[deprecated(since = "soon", note = "use g")]
fn f() {}

fn g() {}
